    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-07-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"instead of","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the instead of meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼が私の代わりに出席しました。”.","hintJa":"「彼が私の代わりに出席しました。」を表す英文と、instead ofの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“My phone died, so I couldn’t call anyone.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「My phone died, so I couldn’t call anyone.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: You couldn’t attend the meeting. What happened?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「会議に出席できなかったのですね。どうなりましたか？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"My phone died, so I couldn’t call anyone.","jp":"携帯の充電が切れて、誰にも連絡できませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"Please bring it tomorrow.","jp":"明日それを持ってきてください。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m good at cooking.","jp":"料理が得意です。"},{"id":"d","en":"Where will she come from?","jp":"彼女はどこから来ますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-07-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"indirect questions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the indirect questions meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女がどこから来るか知っていますか？”.","hintJa":"「彼女がどこから来るか知っていますか？」を表す英文と、indirect questionsの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “Do you know where she will come from?”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「Do you know where she will come from?」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"you know where she will come from?","accepted":["Do you know where she will come from?"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-07-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"bring","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the bring meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “明日それを持ってきてください。”.","hintJa":"「明日それを持ってきてください。」を表す英文と、bringの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Please bring it tomorrow.” directly expresses “明日それを持ってきてください。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「Please bring it tomorrow.」が「明日それを持ってきてください。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 明日それを持ってきてください。","promptJa":"「明日それを持ってきてください。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Please bring it tomorrow.","jp":"明日それを持ってきてください。"},{"id":"b","en":"I brought my notebook.","jp":"ノートを持ってきました。"},{"id":"c","en":"My phone died.","jp":"携帯の充電が切れました。"},{"id":"d","en":"She signed it on my behalf.","jp":"彼女が私の代理で署名しました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-07-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"bring","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A learner arrives in a classroom holding the notebook they brought. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「ノートを持ってきました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A learner arrives in a classroom holding the notebook they brought. That directly matches “I brought my notebook.” (ノートを持ってきました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「ノートを持ってきました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I brought my notebook.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I brought my notebook.","jp":"ノートを持ってきました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I bought a new notebook.","jp":"新しいノートを買いました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Where will she come from?","jp":"彼女はどこから来ますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"Could you do it for me?","jp":"私のためにしてもらえますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-07-01-brought-notebook.webp","imageAlt":"A learner arrives in a classroom holding the notebook they brought.","visualAssetId":"july-07-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-07-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"buy","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A shopper buys a new notebook at a stationery shop. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「新しいノートを買いました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A shopper buys a new notebook at a stationery shop. That directly matches “I bought a new notebook.” (新しいノートを買いました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「新しいノートを買いました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I bought a new notebook.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I bought a new notebook.","jp":"新しいノートを買いました。"},{"id":"b","en":"You told me to do so.","jp":"あなたは私にそうするよう言いました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I got a flat tire.","jp":"タイヤがパンクしました。"},{"id":"d","en":"He attended instead of me.","jp":"彼が私の代わりに出席しました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-07-02-bought-notebook.webp","imageAlt":"A shopper buys a new notebook at a stationery shop.","visualAssetId":"july-07-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-07-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"daily life","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A commuter looks worried at a phone with an empty battery. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「携帯の充電が切れました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A commuter looks worried at a phone with an empty battery. That directly matches “My phone died.” (携帯の充電が切れました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「携帯の充電が切れました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「My phone died.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"My phone died.","jp":"携帯の充電が切れました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Where will she come from?","jp":"彼女はどこから来ますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"She signed it on my behalf.","jp":"彼女が私の代理で署名しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Please bring it tomorrow.","jp":"明日それを持ってきてください。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-07-03-phone-died.webp","imageAlt":"A commuter looks worried at a phone with an empty battery.","visualAssetId":"july-07-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-07-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"travel","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A driver discovers a flat tire beside a parked car. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「タイヤがパンクしました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A driver discovers a flat tire beside a parked car. That directly matches “I got a flat tire.” (タイヤがパンクしました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「タイヤがパンクしました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I got a flat tire.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I got a flat tire.","jp":"タイヤがパンクしました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m good at cooking.","jp":"料理が得意です。"},{"id":"c","en":"He attended instead of me.","jp":"彼が私の代わりに出席しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I bought a new notebook.","jp":"新しいノートを買いました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-07-04-flat-tire.webp","imageAlt":"A driver discovers a flat tire beside a parked car.","visualAssetId":"july-07-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-07', 'july-07-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-07-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"behalf","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A woman signs a document as an authorized representative for a colleague. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「彼女が私の代理で署名しました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A woman signs a document as an authorized representative for a colleague. That directly matches “She signed it on my behalf.” (彼女が私の代理で署名しました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「彼女が私の代理で署名しました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「She signed it on my behalf.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She signed it on my behalf.","jp":"彼女が私の代理で署名しました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Could you do it for me?","jp":"私のためにしてもらえますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Please bring it tomorrow.","jp":"明日それを持ってきてください。"},{"id":"d","en":"My phone died.","jp":"携帯の充電が切れました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-07-05-on-my-behalf.webp","imageAlt":"A woman signs a document as an authorized representative for a colleague.","visualAssetId":"july-07-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-11-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"connected","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the connected meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。”.","hintJa":"「携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。」を表す英文と、connectedの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“My phone is connected to the Wi-Fi.” is the sentence that means “携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「My phone is connected to the Wi-Fi.」が「携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。","promptJa":"「携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"My phone is connected to the Wi-Fi.","jp":"携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I connected the cable.","jp":"ケーブルを接続しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I went back to my hometown.","jp":"地元に帰りました。"},{"id":"d","en":"People sometimes stand close when they talk.","jp":"人は話す時に近くに立つことがあります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-11-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"connect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the connect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ケーブルを接続しました。”.","hintJa":"「ケーブルを接続しました。」を表す英文と、connectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I connected the cable.” is the sentence that means “ケーブルを接続しました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I connected the cable.」が「ケーブルを接続しました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: ケーブルを接続しました。","promptJa":"「ケーブルを接続しました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I connected the cable.","jp":"ケーブルを接続しました。"},{"id":"b","en":"The program is broadcast live.","jp":"その番組は生放送されます。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m staying at my parents’ house.","jp":"実家に泊まっています。"},{"id":"d","en":"The computer was connected yesterday.","jp":"昨日そのパソコンは接続されていました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-11-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"broadcast","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the broadcast meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その番組は生放送されます。”.","hintJa":"「その番組は生放送されます。」を表す英文と、broadcastの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“The program is broadcast live.” is the sentence that means “その番組は生放送されます。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「The program is broadcast live.」が「その番組は生放送されます。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: その番組は生放送されます。","promptJa":"「その番組は生放送されます。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The program is broadcast live.","jp":"その番組は生放送されます。"},{"id":"b","en":"We watched the live stream.","jp":"ライブ配信を見ました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I noticed a strange sound.","jp":"変な音に気づきました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Is the meeting being streamed live?","jp":"会議はライブ配信されていますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-11-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"stream","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the stream meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ライブ配信を見ました。”.","hintJa":"「ライブ配信を見ました。」を表す英文と、streamの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“We watched the live stream.” is the sentence that means “ライブ配信を見ました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「We watched the live stream.」が「ライブ配信を見ました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: ライブ配信を見ました。","promptJa":"「ライブ配信を見ました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"We watched the live stream.","jp":"ライブ配信を見ました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I went back to my hometown.","jp":"地元に帰りました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I realized I had the wrong key.","jp":"違う鍵を持っていると気づきました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I didn’t notice the sign.","jp":"その標識に気づきませんでした。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
