    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-speaking-4', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-11-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"state","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the state meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昨日そのパソコンは接続されていました。”.","hintJa":"「昨日そのパソコンは接続されていました。」を表す英文と、stateの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “The computer was connected yesterday.” (昨日そのパソコンは接続されていました。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「The computer was connected yesterday.」（昨日そのパソコンは接続されていました。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"The computer was connected yesterday.","speakJa":"昨日そのパソコンは接続されていました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-speaking-5', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-11-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"stream","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the stream meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “会議はライブ配信されていますか？”.","hintJa":"「会議はライブ配信されていますか？」を表す英文と、streamの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “Is the meeting being streamed live?” (会議はライブ配信されていますか？). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Is the meeting being streamed live?」（会議はライブ配信されていますか？）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Is the meeting being streamed live?","speakJa":"会議はライブ配信されていますか？"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-11-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"state","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the state meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昨日そのパソコンは接続されていました。”.","hintJa":"「昨日そのパソコンは接続されていました。」を表す英文と、stateの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Yes, it was.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Yes, it was.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Was the computer connected yesterday?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「昨日、そのパソコンは接続されていましたか？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Yes, it was.","jp":"はい、接続されていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Yes, it does.","jp":"はい、そうします。"},{"id":"c","en":"No, I didn’t.","jp":"いいえ、しませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’ll connect it yesterday.","jp":"昨日それを接続します。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-11-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"stream","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the stream meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “会議はライブ配信されていますか？”.","hintJa":"「会議はライブ配信されていますか？」を表す英文と、streamの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “Is the meeting being streamed live?”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「Is the meeting being streamed live?」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"the meeting being streamed live?","accepted":["Is the meeting being streamed live?"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-11-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"notice","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the notice meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その標識に気づきませんでした。”.","hintJa":"「その標識に気づきませんでした。」を表す英文と、noticeの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I didn’t notice the sign.” directly expresses “その標識に気づきませんでした。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I didn’t notice the sign.」が「その標識に気づきませんでした。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: その標識に気づきませんでした。","promptJa":"「その標識に気づきませんでした。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I didn’t notice the sign.","jp":"その標識に気づきませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"My phone is connected to the Wi-Fi.","jp":"携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。"},{"id":"c","en":"We watched the live stream.","jp":"ライブ配信を見ました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I realized I had the wrong key.","jp":"違う鍵を持っていると気づきました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-11-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"connected","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A phone is successfully connected to home Wi-Fi. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A phone is successfully connected to home Wi-Fi. That directly matches “My phone is connected to the Wi-Fi.” (携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。」という場面を表しています。そのため「My phone is connected to the Wi-Fi.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"My phone is connected to the Wi-Fi.","jp":"携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I connected the cable.","jp":"ケーブルを接続しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I went back to my hometown.","jp":"地元に帰りました。"},{"id":"d","en":"People sometimes stand close when they talk.","jp":"人は話す時に近くに立つことがあります。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-11-01-wifi-connected.webp","imageAlt":"A phone is successfully connected to home Wi-Fi.","visualAssetId":"july-11-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-11-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"broadcast","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A television presenter appears in a live broadcast studio. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「その番組は生放送されます。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A television presenter appears in a live broadcast studio. That directly matches “The program is broadcast live.” (その番組は生放送されます。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「その番組は生放送されます。」という場面を表しています。そのため「The program is broadcast live.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The program is broadcast live.","jp":"その番組は生放送されます。"},{"id":"b","en":"We watched the live stream.","jp":"ライブ配信を見ました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I noticed a strange sound.","jp":"変な音に気づきました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Is the meeting being streamed live?","jp":"会議はライブ配信されていますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-11-02-live-broadcast.webp","imageAlt":"A television presenter appears in a live broadcast studio.","visualAssetId":"july-11-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-11-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"hometown","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A traveler returns to their hometown and greets family. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「地元に帰りました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A traveler returns to their hometown and greets family. That directly matches “I went back to my hometown.” (地元に帰りました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「地元に帰りました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I went back to my hometown.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I went back to my hometown.","jp":"地元に帰りました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m staying at my parents’ house.","jp":"実家に泊まっています。"},{"id":"c","en":"People sometimes stand close when they talk.","jp":"人は話す時に近くに立つことがあります。"},{"id":"d","en":"My phone is connected to the Wi-Fi.","jp":"携帯はWi-Fiにつながっています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-11-03-hometown.webp","imageAlt":"A traveler returns to their hometown and greets family.","visualAssetId":"july-11-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-11-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"notice","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person suddenly notices a strange sound from another room. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「変な音に気づきました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person suddenly notices a strange sound from another room. That directly matches “I noticed a strange sound.” (変な音に気づきました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「変な音に気づきました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I noticed a strange sound.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I noticed a strange sound.","jp":"変な音に気づきました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I realized I had the wrong key.","jp":"違う鍵を持っていると気づきました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Is the meeting being streamed live?","jp":"会議はライブ配信されていますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"The program is broadcast live.","jp":"その番組は生放送されます。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-11-04-noticed-sound.webp","imageAlt":"A person suddenly notices a strange sound from another room.","visualAssetId":"july-11-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-11', 'july-11-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-11-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"realize","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person realizes they brought the wrong key at a locked door. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「違う鍵を持っていると気づきました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person realizes they brought the wrong key at a locked door. That directly matches “I realized I had the wrong key.” (違う鍵を持っていると気づきました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「違う鍵を持っていると気づきました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I realized I had the wrong key.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I realized I had the wrong key.","jp":"違う鍵を持っていると気づきました。"},{"id":"b","en":"People sometimes stand close when they talk.","jp":"人は話す時に近くに立つことがあります。"},{"id":"c","en":"I didn’t notice the sign.","jp":"その標識に気づきませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"We watched the live stream.","jp":"ライブ配信を見ました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-11-05-wrong-key.webp","imageAlt":"A person realizes they brought the wrong key at a locked door.","visualAssetId":"july-11-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-12-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “まだお酒を飲んでいません。”.","hintJa":"「まだお酒を飲んでいません。」を表す英文と、present perfectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I haven’t had any alcohol yet.” is the sentence that means “まだお酒を飲んでいません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I haven’t had any alcohol yet.」が「まだお酒を飲んでいません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: まだお酒を飲んでいません。","promptJa":"「まだお酒を飲んでいません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I haven’t had any alcohol yet.","jp":"まだお酒を飲んでいません。"},{"id":"b","en":"Have you had lunch yet?","jp":"もう昼食を食べましたか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I didn’t drink yesterday.","jp":"昨日は飲みませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"Have you ever had Malaysian food?","jp":"マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-12-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう昼食を食べましたか？”.","hintJa":"「もう昼食を食べましたか？」を表す英文と、present perfectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Have you had lunch yet?” is the sentence that means “もう昼食を食べましたか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Have you had lunch yet?」が「もう昼食を食べましたか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: もう昼食を食べましたか？","promptJa":"「もう昼食を食べましたか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Have you had lunch yet?","jp":"もう昼食を食べましたか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I had lunch at noon.","jp":"正午に昼食を食べました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I haven’t eaten anything today.","jp":"今日はまだ何も食べていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’ve had this bag for years.","jp":"この鞄を何年も持っています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-12-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “正午に昼食を食べました。”.","hintJa":"「正午に昼食を食べました。」を表す英文と、pastの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I had lunch at noon.” is the sentence that means “正午に昼食を食べました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I had lunch at noon.」が「正午に昼食を食べました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 正午に昼食を食べました。","promptJa":"「正午に昼食を食べました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I had lunch at noon.","jp":"正午に昼食を食べました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I don’t drink alcohol.","jp":"私はお酒を飲みません。"},{"id":"c","en":"She has already had breakfast.","jp":"彼女はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"d","en":"He hasn’t had any coffee.","jp":"彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-12-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"habit","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the habit meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はお酒を飲みません。”.","hintJa":"「私はお酒を飲みません。」を表す英文と、habitの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I don’t drink alcohol.” is the sentence that means “私はお酒を飲みません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I don’t drink alcohol.」が「私はお酒を飲みません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 私はお酒を飲みません。","promptJa":"「私はお酒を飲みません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I don’t drink alcohol.","jp":"私はお酒を飲みません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I didn’t drink yesterday.","jp":"昨日は飲みませんでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"We haven’t decided yet.","jp":"まだ決めていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"They had dinner last night.","jp":"昨夜夕食を食べました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-12-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昨日は飲みませんでした。”.","hintJa":"「昨日は飲みませんでした。」を表す英文と、pastの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"True. “I didn’t drink yesterday.” means “昨日は飲みませんでした。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「I didn’t drink yesterday.」は「昨日は飲みませんでした。」という意味です。","prompt":"“I didn’t drink yesterday.” means “昨日は飲みませんでした。”.","promptJa":"「I didn’t drink yesterday.」は「昨日は飲みませんでした。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-12-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"any","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the any meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今日はまだ何も食べていません。”.","hintJa":"「今日はまだ何も食べていません。」を表す英文と、anyの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"False. “I haven’t eaten anything today.” means “今日はまだ何も食べていません。”, not “彼女はもう朝食を食べました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I haven’t eaten anything today.」は「今日はまだ何も食べていません。」であり、「彼女はもう朝食を食べました。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I haven’t eaten anything today.” means “彼女はもう朝食を食べました。”.","promptJa":"「I haven’t eaten anything today.」は「彼女はもう朝食を食べました。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-12-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"already","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the already meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女はもう朝食を食べました。”.","hintJa":"「彼女はもう朝食を食べました。」を表す英文と、alreadyの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"A natural translation is “She has already had breakfast.”. It expresses “彼女はもう朝食を食べました。” with the lesson’s already pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「She has already had breakfast.」です。「彼女はもう朝食を食べました。」を今回のalready表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 彼女はもう朝食を食べました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：彼女はもう朝食を食べました。","accepted":["She has already had breakfast."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-12-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"yet","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the yet meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “まだ決めていません。”.","hintJa":"「まだ決めていません。」を表す英文と、yetの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"A natural translation is “We haven’t decided yet.”. It expresses “まだ決めていません。” with the lesson’s yet pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「We haven’t decided yet.」です。「まだ決めていません。」を今回のyet表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: まだ決めていません。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：まだ決めていません。","accepted":["We haven’t decided yet."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-order-1', 8, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"july-12-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"experience","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the experience meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？”.","hintJa":"「マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？」を表す英文と、experienceの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct order: “Have you ever had Malaysian food?”. Build the sentence around the experience pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「Have you ever had Malaysian food?」です。experienceの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？","words":["had","Malaysian","food","Have","you","ever"],"correctWords":["Have","you","ever","had","Malaysian","food"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
