    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-speaking-1', 18, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-12-draft-speaking-1","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “正午に昼食を食べました。”.","hintJa":"「正午に昼食を食べました。」を表す英文と、pastの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I had lunch at noon.” (正午に昼食を食べました。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I had lunch at noon.」（正午に昼食を食べました。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I had lunch at noon.","speakJa":"正午に昼食を食べました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-speaking-2', 19, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-12-draft-speaking-2","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"any","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the any meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今日はまだ何も食べていません。”.","hintJa":"「今日はまだ何も食べていません。」を表す英文と、anyの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I haven’t eaten anything today.” (今日はまだ何も食べていません。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I haven’t eaten anything today.」（今日はまだ何も食べていません。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I haven’t eaten anything today.","speakJa":"今日はまだ何も食べていません。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-speaking-3', 20, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-12-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"experience","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the experience meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？”.","hintJa":"「マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？」を表す英文と、experienceの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “Have you ever had Malaysian food?” (マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Have you ever had Malaysian food?」（マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"Have you ever had Malaysian food?","speakJa":"マレーシア料理を食べたことがありますか？"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-speaking-4', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-12-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"continuation","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the continuation meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この鞄を何年も持っています。”.","hintJa":"「この鞄を何年も持っています。」を表す英文と、continuationの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I’ve had this bag for years.” (この鞄を何年も持っています。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I’ve had this bag for years.」（この鞄を何年も持っています。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I’ve had this bag for years.","speakJa":"この鞄を何年も持っています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-speaking-5', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-12-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"any","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the any meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。”.","hintJa":"「彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。」を表す英文と、anyの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “He hasn’t had any coffee.” (彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「He hasn’t had any coffee.」（彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"He hasn’t had any coffee.","speakJa":"彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-12-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"continuation","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the continuation meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この鞄を何年も持っています。”.","hintJa":"「この鞄を何年も持っています。」を表す英文と、continuationの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I’ve had this bag for years.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I’ve had this bag for years.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Is that bag new?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「その鞄は新しいですか？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve had this bag for years.","jp":"この鞄を何年も持っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"He hasn’t had any coffee.","jp":"彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。"},{"id":"c","en":"Have you had lunch yet?","jp":"もう昼食を食べましたか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t eaten anything today.","jp":"今日はまだ何も食べていません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-12-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"any","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the any meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。”.","hintJa":"「彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。」を表す英文と、anyの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “He hasn’t had any coffee.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「He hasn’t had any coffee.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"He had any coffee.","accepted":["He hasn’t had any coffee."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-12-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昨夜夕食を食べました。”.","hintJa":"「昨夜夕食を食べました。」を表す英文と、pastの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“They had dinner last night.” directly expresses “昨夜夕食を食べました。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「They had dinner last night.」が「昨夜夕食を食べました。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 昨夜夕食を食べました。","promptJa":"「昨夜夕食を食べました。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"They had dinner last night.","jp":"昨夜夕食を食べました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t had any alcohol yet.","jp":"まだお酒を飲んでいません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I don’t drink alcohol.","jp":"私はお酒を飲みません。"},{"id":"d","en":"We haven’t decided yet.","jp":"まだ決めていません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-12-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person eats lunch at noon. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「正午に昼食を食べました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person eats lunch at noon. That directly matches “I had lunch at noon.” (正午に昼食を食べました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「正午に昼食を食べました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I had lunch at noon.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I had lunch at noon.","jp":"正午に昼食を食べました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I don’t drink alcohol.","jp":"私はお酒を飲みません。"},{"id":"c","en":"She has already had breakfast.","jp":"彼女はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"d","en":"He hasn’t had any coffee.","jp":"彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-12-01-lunch-noon.webp","imageAlt":"A person eats lunch at noon.","visualAssetId":"july-12-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-12-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"any","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A hungry person has an empty lunchbox late in the day. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「今日はまだ何も食べていません。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A hungry person has an empty lunchbox late in the day. That directly matches “I haven’t eaten anything today.” (今日はまだ何も食べていません。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「今日はまだ何も食べていません。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I haven’t eaten anything today.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I haven’t eaten anything today.","jp":"今日はまだ何も食べていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"She has already had breakfast.","jp":"彼女はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve had this bag for years.","jp":"この鞄を何年も持っています。"},{"id":"d","en":"Have you had lunch yet?","jp":"もう昼食を食べましたか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-12-02-not-eaten-today.webp","imageAlt":"A hungry person has an empty lunchbox late in the day.","visualAssetId":"july-12-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-12-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"already","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A satisfied woman has already finished breakfast. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「彼女はもう朝食を食べました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A satisfied woman has already finished breakfast. That directly matches “She has already had breakfast.” (彼女はもう朝食を食べました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「彼女はもう朝食を食べました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「She has already had breakfast.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She has already had breakfast.","jp":"彼女はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"b","en":"We haven’t decided yet.","jp":"まだ決めていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"He hasn’t had any coffee.","jp":"彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I had lunch at noon.","jp":"正午に昼食を食べました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-12-03-breakfast-already.webp","imageAlt":"A satisfied woman has already finished breakfast.","visualAssetId":"july-12-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-12-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"continuation","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: The same well-loved bag is used over many years. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「この鞄を何年も持っています。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: The same well-loved bag is used over many years. That directly matches “I’ve had this bag for years.” (この鞄を何年も持っています。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「この鞄を何年も持っています。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I’ve had this bag for years.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve had this bag for years.","jp":"この鞄を何年も持っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"He hasn’t had any coffee.","jp":"彼はまだコーヒーを飲んでいません。"},{"id":"c","en":"Have you had lunch yet?","jp":"もう昼食を食べましたか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t eaten anything today.","jp":"今日はまだ何も食べていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-12-04-bag-for-years.webp","imageAlt":"The same well-loved bag is used over many years.","visualAssetId":"july-12-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-12', 'july-12-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-12-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: Friends ate dinner together last night. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「昨夜夕食を食べました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: Friends ate dinner together last night. That directly matches “They had dinner last night.” (昨夜夕食を食べました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「昨夜夕食を食べました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「They had dinner last night.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"They had dinner last night.","jp":"昨夜夕食を食べました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t had any alcohol yet.","jp":"まだお酒を飲んでいません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I don’t drink alcohol.","jp":"私はお酒を飲みません。"},{"id":"d","en":"We haven’t decided yet.","jp":"まだ決めていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-12-05-dinner-last-night.webp","imageAlt":"Friends ate dinner together last night.","visualAssetId":"july-12-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-13', 'july-13-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-13-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"possibility","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the possibility meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。”.","hintJa":"「この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。」を表す英文と、possibilityの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Someone might call me around this time.” is the sentence that means “この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Someone might call me around this time.」が「この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。","promptJa":"「この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Someone might call me around this time.","jp":"この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。"},{"id":"b","en":"No one usually calls me at this time.","jp":"この時間には普段誰も電話しません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I need to rush back.","jp":"急いで戻る必要があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"The streets are packed with people.","jp":"通りは人でいっぱいです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-13', 'july-13-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-13-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"time","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the time meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この時間には普段誰も電話しません。”.","hintJa":"「この時間には普段誰も電話しません。」を表す英文と、timeの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“No one usually calls me at this time.” is the sentence that means “この時間には普段誰も電話しません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「No one usually calls me at this time.」が「この時間には普段誰も電話しません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: この時間には普段誰も電話しません。","promptJa":"「この時間には普段誰も電話しません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"No one usually calls me at this time.","jp":"この時間には普段誰も電話しません。"},{"id":"b","en":"My signal is weak.","jp":"電波が弱いです。"},{"id":"c","en":"That’s unusual.","jp":"それは珍しいですね。"},{"id":"d","en":"It feels long at the beginning of the week.","jp":"週の初めは長く感じます。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-13', 'july-13-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-13-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"technology","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the technology meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “電波が弱いです。”.","hintJa":"「電波が弱いです。」を表す英文と、technologyの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“My signal is weak.” is the sentence that means “電波が弱いです。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「My signal is weak.」が「電波が弱いです。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 電波が弱いです。","promptJa":"「電波が弱いです。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"My signal is weak.","jp":"電波が弱いです。"},{"id":"b","en":"The Wi-Fi connection is unstable.","jp":"Wi-Fi接続が不安定です。"},{"id":"c","en":"This shop doesn’t have tiramisu, but that one does.","jp":"この店にはティラミスがありませんが、あちらにはあります。"},{"id":"d","en":"Will you be there this time?","jp":"今回はそこにいますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
