    ('july-13', 'july-13-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-13-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"possibility","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person watches the clock while expecting a possible phone call. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person watches the clock while expecting a possible phone call. That directly matches “Someone might call me around this time.” (この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。」という場面を表しています。そのため「Someone might call me around this time.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Someone might call me around this time.","jp":"この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。"},{"id":"b","en":"No one usually calls me at this time.","jp":"この時間には普段誰も電話しません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I need to rush back.","jp":"急いで戻る必要があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"The streets are packed with people.","jp":"通りは人でいっぱいです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-13-01-expected-call.webp","imageAlt":"A person watches the clock while expecting a possible phone call.","visualAssetId":"july-13-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-13', 'july-13-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-13-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"technology","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A phone has a weak mobile signal. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「電波が弱いです。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A phone has a weak mobile signal. That directly matches “My signal is weak.” (電波が弱いです。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「電波が弱いです。」という場面を表しています。そのため「My signal is weak.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"My signal is weak.","jp":"電波が弱いです。"},{"id":"b","en":"The Wi-Fi connection is unstable.","jp":"Wi-Fi接続が不安定です。"},{"id":"c","en":"This shop doesn’t have tiramisu, but that one does.","jp":"この店にはティラミスがありませんが、あちらにはあります。"},{"id":"d","en":"Will you be there this time?","jp":"今回はそこにいますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-13-02-weak-signal.webp","imageAlt":"A phone has a weak mobile signal.","visualAssetId":"july-13-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-13', 'july-13-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-13-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"movement","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person rushes back toward an office after forgetting something. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「急いで戻る必要があります。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person rushes back toward an office after forgetting something. That directly matches “I need to rush back.” (急いで戻る必要があります。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「急いで戻る必要があります。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I need to rush back.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I need to rush back.","jp":"急いで戻る必要があります。"},{"id":"b","en":"That’s unusual.","jp":"それは珍しいですね。"},{"id":"c","en":"The streets are packed with people.","jp":"通りは人でいっぱいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Someone might call me around this time.","jp":"この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-13-03-rush-back.webp","imageAlt":"A person rushes back toward an office after forgetting something.","visualAssetId":"july-13-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-13', 'july-13-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-13-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"time","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: Calendar pages seem to fly past during a quick week. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「一週間が早く過ぎました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: Calendar pages seem to fly past during a quick week. That directly matches “The week went by quickly.” (一週間が早く過ぎました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「一週間が早く過ぎました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「The week went by quickly.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The week went by quickly.","jp":"一週間が早く過ぎました。"},{"id":"b","en":"The streets are packed with people.","jp":"通りは人でいっぱいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"There are many people walking in Tokyo.","jp":"東京では多くの人が歩いています。"},{"id":"d","en":"The Wi-Fi connection is unstable.","jp":"Wi-Fi接続が不安定です。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-13-04-week-flew-by.webp","imageAlt":"Calendar pages seem to fly past during a quick week.","visualAssetId":"july-13-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-13', 'july-13-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-13-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"city","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A city street is packed with pedestrians. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「通りは人でいっぱいです。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A city street is packed with pedestrians. That directly matches “The streets are packed with people.” (通りは人でいっぱいです。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「通りは人でいっぱいです。」という場面を表しています。そのため「The streets are packed with people.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The streets are packed with people.","jp":"通りは人でいっぱいです。"},{"id":"b","en":"It feels long at the beginning of the week.","jp":"週の初めは長く感じます。"},{"id":"c","en":"Someone might call me around this time.","jp":"この時間帯に誰かが電話するかもしれません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I need to rush back.","jp":"急いで戻る必要があります。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-13-05-packed-street.webp","imageAlt":"A city street is packed with pedestrians.","visualAssetId":"july-13-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-18-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"supposed to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the supposed to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そのクラスに参加する予定でした。”.","hintJa":"「そのクラスに参加する予定でした。」を表す英文と、supposed toの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I was supposed to join the class.” is the sentence that means “そのクラスに参加する予定でした。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I was supposed to join the class.」が「そのクラスに参加する予定でした。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: そのクラスに参加する予定でした。","promptJa":"「そのクラスに参加する予定でした。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I was supposed to join the class.","jp":"そのクラスに参加する予定でした。"},{"id":"b","en":"She has a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I do like this song.","jp":"この歌は本当に好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"He’s on fire today.","jp":"彼は今日は絶好調です。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-18-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"has","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the has meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は猫を飼っています。”.","hintJa":"「彼女は猫を飼っています。」を表す英文と、hasの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“She has a cat.” is the sentence that means “彼女は猫を飼っています。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「She has a cat.」が「彼女は猫を飼っています。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼女は猫を飼っています。","promptJa":"「彼女は猫を飼っています。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She has a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"She doesn’t have a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"The pot was on the stove.","jp":"鍋はコンロにかかっていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I have a driver’s license.","jp":"運転免許を持っています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-18-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"doesn''t have","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the doesn''t have meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は猫を飼っていません。”.","hintJa":"「彼女は猫を飼っていません。」を表す英文と、doesn''t haveの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“She doesn’t have a cat.” is the sentence that means “彼女は猫を飼っていません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「She doesn’t have a cat.」が「彼女は猫を飼っていません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼女は猫を飼っていません。","promptJa":"「彼女は猫を飼っていません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She doesn’t have a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"She hasn’t eaten yet.","jp":"彼女はまだ食べていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"The pot caught fire.","jp":"鍋に火がつきました。"},{"id":"d","en":"We’re supposed to meet at ten.","jp":"10時に会うことになっています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-18-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"hasn''t","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the hasn''t meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女はまだ食べていません。”.","hintJa":"「彼女はまだ食べていません。」を表す英文と、hasn''tの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“She hasn’t eaten yet.” is the sentence that means “彼女はまだ食べていません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「She hasn’t eaten yet.」が「彼女はまだ食べていません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼女はまだ食べていません。","promptJa":"「彼女はまだ食べていません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She hasn’t eaten yet.","jp":"彼女はまだ食べていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I do like this song.","jp":"この歌は本当に好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"The house is on fire.","jp":"家が燃えています。"},{"id":"d","en":"She’s fired up and ready.","jp":"彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
