    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-speaking-4', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-18-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"have","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the have meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “運転免許を持っています。”.","hintJa":"「運転免許を持っています。」を表す英文と、haveの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I have a driver’s license.” (運転免許を持っています。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I have a driver’s license.」（運転免許を持っています。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I have a driver’s license.","speakJa":"運転免許を持っています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-speaking-5', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-18-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"supposed to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the supposed to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “10時に会うことになっています。”.","hintJa":"「10時に会うことになっています。」を表す英文と、supposed toの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “We’re supposed to meet at ten.” (10時に会うことになっています。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「We’re supposed to meet at ten.」（10時に会うことになっています。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"We’re supposed to meet at ten.","speakJa":"10時に会うことになっています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-18-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"have","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the have meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “運転免許を持っています。”.","hintJa":"「運転免許を持っています。」を表す英文と、haveの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Yes, I can. I have a driver’s license.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Yes, I can. I have a driver’s license.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Can you drive?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「運転できますか？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Yes, I can. I have a driver’s license.","jp":"はい、できます。運転免許を持っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"Yes, I do drive yesterday.","jp":"はい、昨日運転します。"},{"id":"c","en":"No, I haven’t a license.","jp":"いいえ、免許を持っていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m supposed at ten.","jp":"10時に予定されています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-18-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"supposed to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the supposed to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “10時に会うことになっています。”.","hintJa":"「10時に会うことになっています。」を表す英文と、supposed toの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “We’re supposed to meet at ten.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「We’re supposed to meet at ten.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"We supposed to meet at ten.","accepted":["We’re supposed to meet at ten."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-18-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feelings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。”.","hintJa":"「彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。」を表す英文と、feelingsの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“She’s fired up and ready.” directly expresses “彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「She’s fired up and ready.」が「彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。","promptJa":"「彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She’s fired up and ready.","jp":"彼女は気合いが入って準備万端です。"},{"id":"b","en":"I was supposed to join the class.","jp":"そのクラスに参加する予定でした。"},{"id":"c","en":"She hasn’t eaten yet.","jp":"彼女はまだ食べていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"The house is on fire.","jp":"家が燃えています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-18', 'july-18-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-18-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"has","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A woman happily holds her pet cat at home. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「彼女は猫を飼っています。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A woman happily holds her pet cat at home. That directly matches “She has a cat.” (彼女は猫を飼っています。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「彼女は猫を飼っています。」という場面を表しています。そのため「She has a cat.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She has a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"She doesn’t have a cat.","jp":"彼女は猫を飼っていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"The pot was on the stove.","jp":"鍋はコンロにかかっていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I have a driver’s license.","jp":"運転免許を持っています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-18-01-has-cat.webp","imageAlt":"A woman happily holds her pet cat at home.","visualAssetId":"july-18-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
