    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-speaking-4', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-19-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"on my way","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the on my way meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “仕事へ向かっている途中です。”.","hintJa":"「仕事へ向かっている途中です。」を表す英文と、on my wayの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I’m on my way to work.” (仕事へ向かっている途中です。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I’m on my way to work.」（仕事へ向かっている途中です。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I’m on my way to work.","speakJa":"仕事へ向かっている途中です。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-speaking-5', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-19-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"won''t","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the won''t meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “コーヒーは飲みません。”.","hintJa":"「コーヒーは飲みません。」を表す英文と、won''tの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “I won’t have coffee.” (コーヒーは飲みません。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I won’t have coffee.」（コーヒーは飲みません。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I won’t have coffee.","speakJa":"コーヒーは飲みません。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-19-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"on my way","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the on my way meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “仕事へ向かっている途中です。”.","hintJa":"「仕事へ向かっている途中です。」を表す英文と、on my wayの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I’m on my way to work.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I’m on my way to work.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Where are you now?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「今どこにいますか？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m on my way to work.","jp":"仕事へ向かっている途中です。"},{"id":"b","en":"I won’t have coffee.","jp":"コーヒーは飲みません。"},{"id":"c","en":"Either day works for me.","jp":"どちらの日でも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’d rather not talk about it.","jp":"できればその話はしたくありません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-19-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"won''t","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the won''t meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “コーヒーは飲みません。”.","hintJa":"「コーヒーは飲みません。」を表す英文と、won''tの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “I won’t have coffee.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「I won’t have coffee.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"I won have coffee.","accepted":["I won’t have coffee."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-19-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"want","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the want meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “コーヒーを飲みたいです。”.","hintJa":"「コーヒーを飲みたいです。」を表す英文と、wantの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I want to have coffee.” directly expresses “コーヒーを飲みたいです。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I want to have coffee.」が「コーヒーを飲みたいです。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: コーヒーを飲みたいです。","promptJa":"「コーヒーを飲みたいです。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I want to have coffee.","jp":"コーヒーを飲みたいです。"},{"id":"b","en":"I like both tea and coffee.","jp":"紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I don’t like either.","jp":"どちらも好きではありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"That joke cracked me up.","jp":"その冗談で爆笑しました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-19-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"both","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person happily chooses both tea and coffee. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person happily chooses both tea and coffee. That directly matches “I like both tea and coffee.” (紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I like both tea and coffee.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I like both tea and coffee.","jp":"紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Either day works for me.","jp":"どちらの日でも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’d rather stay home than go out.","jp":"外出するより家にいたいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I ran into an old friend.","jp":"昔の友人に偶然会いました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-19-01-both-drinks.webp","imageAlt":"A person happily chooses both tea and coffee.","visualAssetId":"july-19-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-19-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"either","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person is equally available on either of two calendar days. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「どちらの日でも大丈夫です。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person is equally available on either of two calendar days. That directly matches “Either day works for me.” (どちらの日でも大丈夫です。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「どちらの日でも大丈夫です。」という場面を表しています。そのため「Either day works for me.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Either day works for me.","jp":"どちらの日でも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"b","en":"I like neither option.","jp":"どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’d rather not talk about it.","jp":"できればその話はしたくありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m on my way to work.","jp":"仕事へ向かっている途中です。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-19-02-either-day.webp","imageAlt":"A person is equally available on either of two calendar days.","visualAssetId":"july-19-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-19-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"neither","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person rejects both of two options. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person rejects both of two options. That directly matches “I like neither option.” (どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I like neither option.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I like neither option.","jp":"どちらの選択肢も好きではありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’d rather stay home than go out.","jp":"外出するより家にいたいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"That was hilarious.","jp":"それは爆笑するほど面白かったです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I won’t have coffee.","jp":"コーヒーは飲みません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-19-03-neither-option.webp","imageAlt":"A person rejects both of two options.","visualAssetId":"july-19-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-19-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"would rather","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person prefers relaxing at home instead of going out. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「外出するより家にいたいです。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person prefers relaxing at home instead of going out. That directly matches “I’d rather stay home than go out.” (外出するより家にいたいです。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「外出するより家にいたいです。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I’d rather stay home than go out.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’d rather stay home than go out.","jp":"外出するより家にいたいです。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’d rather not talk about it.","jp":"できればその話はしたくありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I ran into an old friend.","jp":"昔の友人に偶然会いました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I like both tea and coffee.","jp":"紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-19-04-rather-home.webp","imageAlt":"A person prefers relaxing at home instead of going out.","visualAssetId":"july-19-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-19', 'july-19-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-19-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"run into","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: Two old friends unexpectedly meet on a city sidewalk. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「昔の友人に偶然会いました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: Two old friends unexpectedly meet on a city sidewalk. That directly matches “I ran into an old friend.” (昔の友人に偶然会いました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「昔の友人に偶然会いました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I ran into an old friend.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I ran into an old friend.","jp":"昔の友人に偶然会いました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m on my way to work.","jp":"仕事へ向かっている途中です。"},{"id":"c","en":"I like both tea and coffee.","jp":"紅茶もコーヒーも両方好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’d rather stay home than go out.","jp":"外出するより家にいたいです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-19-05-ran-into-friend.webp","imageAlt":"Two old friends unexpectedly meet on a city sidewalk.","visualAssetId":"july-19-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-22-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"availability","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the availability meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？”.","hintJa":"「8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？」を表す英文と、availabilityの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?” is the sentence that means “8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?」が「8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？","promptJa":"「8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","jp":"8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Are you guys ready?","jp":"皆さん、準備はできましたか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Neither is okay.","jp":"どちらも駄目です。"},{"id":"d","en":"That’s right. I don’t like it.","jp":"その通りです。好きではありません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-22-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"you guys","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the you guys meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “皆さん、準備はできましたか？”.","hintJa":"「皆さん、準備はできましたか？」を表す英文と、you guysの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Are you guys ready?” is the sentence that means “皆さん、準備はできましたか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Are you guys ready?」が「皆さん、準備はできましたか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 皆さん、準備はできましたか？","promptJa":"「皆さん、準備はできましたか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Are you guys ready?","jp":"皆さん、準備はできましたか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I like both.","jp":"両方好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I prefer cucumber to eggplant.","jp":"ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Actually, I do like it.","jp":"実は本当に好きです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-22-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"both","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the both meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “両方好きです。”.","hintJa":"「両方好きです。」を表す英文と、bothの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I like both.” is the sentence that means “両方好きです。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I like both.」が「両方好きです。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 両方好きです。","promptJa":"「両方好きです。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I like both.","jp":"両方好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Either is fine.","jp":"どちらでも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"c","en":"Yes, I do. I like yakiniku.","jp":"はい、焼肉が好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Night shifts are still better.","jp":"それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-22-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"either","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the either meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どちらでも大丈夫です。”.","hintJa":"「どちらでも大丈夫です。」を表す英文と、eitherの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Either is fine.” is the sentence that means “どちらでも大丈夫です。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Either is fine.」が「どちらでも大丈夫です。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: どちらでも大丈夫です。","promptJa":"「どちらでも大丈夫です。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Either is fine.","jp":"どちらでも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"b","en":"Neither is okay.","jp":"どちらも駄目です。"},{"id":"c","en":"No, I don’t. I don’t like it.","jp":"いいえ、好きではありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Is the meeting room available?","jp":"会議室は利用できますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-22-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"neither","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the neither meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どちらも駄目です。”.","hintJa":"「どちらも駄目です。」を表す英文と、neitherの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"True. “Neither is okay.” means “どちらも駄目です。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「Neither is okay.」は「どちらも駄目です。」という意味です。","prompt":"“Neither is okay.” means “どちらも駄目です。”.","promptJa":"「Neither is okay.」は「どちらも駄目です。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-22-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"prefer","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the prefer meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。”.","hintJa":"「ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。」を表す英文と、preferの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"False. “I prefer cucumber to eggplant.” means “ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。”, not “はい、焼肉が好きです。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I prefer cucumber to eggplant.」は「ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。」であり、「はい、焼肉が好きです。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I prefer cucumber to eggplant.” means “はい、焼肉が好きです。”.","promptJa":"「I prefer cucumber to eggplant.」は「はい、焼肉が好きです。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-22-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"answers","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the answers meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “はい、焼肉が好きです。”.","hintJa":"「はい、焼肉が好きです。」を表す英文と、answersの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"A natural translation is “Yes, I do. I like yakiniku.”. It expresses “はい、焼肉が好きです。” with the lesson’s answers pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「Yes, I do. I like yakiniku.」です。「はい、焼肉が好きです。」を今回のanswers表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: はい、焼肉が好きです。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：はい、焼肉が好きです。","accepted":["Yes, I do. I like yakiniku."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-22-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"answers","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the answers meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “いいえ、好きではありません。”.","hintJa":"「いいえ、好きではありません。」を表す英文と、answersの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"A natural translation is “No, I don’t. I don’t like it.”. It expresses “いいえ、好きではありません。” with the lesson’s answers pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「No, I don’t. I don’t like it.」です。「いいえ、好きではありません。」を今回のanswers表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: いいえ、好きではありません。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：いいえ、好きではありません。","accepted":["No, I don’t. I don’t like it."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-order-1', 8, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"july-22-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"right","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the right meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その通りです。好きではありません。”.","hintJa":"「その通りです。好きではありません。」を表す英文と、rightの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct order: “That’s right. I don’t like it.”. Build the sentence around the right pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「That’s right. I don’t like it.」です。rightの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: その通りです。好きではありません。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：その通りです。好きではありません。","words":["don’t","like","it","That’s","right","I"],"correctWords":["That’s","right","I","don’t","like","it"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-order-2', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"july-22-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"emphasis","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the emphasis meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “実は本当に好きです。”.","hintJa":"「実は本当に好きです。」を表す英文と、emphasisの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct order: “Actually, I do like it.”. Build the sentence around the emphasis pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「Actually, I do like it.」です。emphasisの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 実は本当に好きです。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：実は本当に好きです。","words":["I","it","do","Actually,","like"],"correctWords":["Actually,","I","do","like","it"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-matching', 10, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"july-22-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"availability","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the availability meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？”.","hintJa":"「8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？」を表す英文と、availabilityの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","jp":"8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？","cat":"availability"},{"en":"Are you guys ready?","jp":"皆さん、準備はできましたか？","cat":"you guys"},{"en":"I like both.","jp":"両方好きです。","cat":"both"},{"en":"Either is fine.","jp":"どちらでも大丈夫です。","cat":"either"},{"en":"Neither is okay.","jp":"どちらも駄目です。","cat":"neither"},{"en":"I prefer cucumber to eggplant.","jp":"ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。","cat":"prefer"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-sorting', 11, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"july-22-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"you guys","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the you guys meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “皆さん、準備はできましたか？”.","hintJa":"「皆さん、準備はできましたか？」を表す英文と、you guysの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are availability, you guys, both.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「availability・you guys・both」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["availability","you guys","both"],"items":[["Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","availability"],["Are you guys ready?","you guys"],["I like both.","both"]]}'::jsonb, false, 3),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-listen-choice-1', 12, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"july-22-draft-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"availability","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the availability meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？”.","hintJa":"「8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？」を表す英文と、availabilityの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","jp":"8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Are you guys ready?","jp":"皆さん、準備はできましたか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Neither is okay.","jp":"どちらも駄目です。"},{"id":"d","en":"That’s right. I don’t like it.","jp":"その通りです。好きではありません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-listen-choice-2', 13, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"july-22-draft-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"either","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the either meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どちらでも大丈夫です。”.","hintJa":"「どちらでも大丈夫です。」を表す英文と、eitherの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “Either is fine.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「Either is fine.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"Either is fine.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Either is fine.","jp":"どちらでも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"b","en":"Neither is okay.","jp":"どちらも駄目です。"},{"id":"c","en":"No, I don’t. I don’t like it.","jp":"いいえ、好きではありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Is the meeting room available?","jp":"会議室は利用できますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
