    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-speaking-5', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-22-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"still","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the still meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。”.","hintJa":"「それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。」を表す英文と、stillの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “Night shifts are still better.” (それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Night shifts are still better.」（それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Night shifts are still better.","speakJa":"それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-22-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"emphasis","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the emphasis meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “実は本当に好きです。”.","hintJa":"「実は本当に好きです。」を表す英文と、emphasisの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Actually, I do like it.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Actually, I do like it.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: You don’t like yakiniku, right?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「焼肉が好きじゃないんですよね？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Actually, I do like it.","jp":"実は本当に好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Night shifts are still better.","jp":"それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"Are you guys ready?","jp":"皆さん、準備はできましたか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I prefer cucumber to eggplant.","jp":"ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-22-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"still","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the still meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。”.","hintJa":"「それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。」を表す英文と、stillの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “Night shifts are still better.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「Night shifts are still better.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"Night shifts still better.","accepted":["Night shifts are still better."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-22-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"available","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the available meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “会議室は利用できますか？”.","hintJa":"「会議室は利用できますか？」を表す英文と、availableの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Is the meeting room available?” directly expresses “会議室は利用できますか？”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「Is the meeting room available?」が「会議室は利用できますか？」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 会議室は利用できますか？","promptJa":"「会議室は利用できますか？」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Is the meeting room available?","jp":"会議室は利用できますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","jp":"8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Either is fine.","jp":"どちらでも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"d","en":"No, I don’t. I don’t like it.","jp":"いいえ、好きではありません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-22-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"availability","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person checks whether a morning appointment time is available. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person checks whether a morning appointment time is available. That directly matches “Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?” (8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？」という場面を表しています。そのため「Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","jp":"8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Are you guys ready?","jp":"皆さん、準備はできましたか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Neither is okay.","jp":"どちらも駄目です。"},{"id":"d","en":"That’s right. I don’t like it.","jp":"その通りです。好きではありません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-22-01-availability.webp","imageAlt":"A person checks whether a morning appointment time is available.","visualAssetId":"july-22-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-22-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"you guys","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A group is ready to leave together. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「皆さん、準備はできましたか？」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A group is ready to leave together. That directly matches “Are you guys ready?” (皆さん、準備はできましたか？); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「皆さん、準備はできましたか？」という場面を表しています。そのため「Are you guys ready?」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Are you guys ready?","jp":"皆さん、準備はできましたか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I like both.","jp":"両方好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I prefer cucumber to eggplant.","jp":"ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Actually, I do like it.","jp":"実は本当に好きです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-22-02-group-ready.webp","imageAlt":"A group is ready to leave together.","visualAssetId":"july-22-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-22-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"both","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A diner happily likes both dishes. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「両方好きです。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A diner happily likes both dishes. That directly matches “I like both.” (両方好きです。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「両方好きです。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I like both.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I like both.","jp":"両方好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Either is fine.","jp":"どちらでも大丈夫です。"},{"id":"c","en":"Yes, I do. I like yakiniku.","jp":"はい、焼肉が好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Night shifts are still better.","jp":"それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-22-03-like-both.webp","imageAlt":"A diner happily likes both dishes.","visualAssetId":"july-22-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-22-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"neither","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: Neither of two damaged items is acceptable. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「どちらも駄目です。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: Neither of two damaged items is acceptable. That directly matches “Neither is okay.” (どちらも駄目です。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「どちらも駄目です。」という場面を表しています。そのため「Neither is okay.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Neither is okay.","jp":"どちらも駄目です。"},{"id":"b","en":"I prefer cucumber to eggplant.","jp":"ナスよりキュウリの方が好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"That’s right. I don’t like it.","jp":"その通りです。好きではありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","jp":"8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-22-04-neither-okay.webp","imageAlt":"Neither of two damaged items is acceptable.","visualAssetId":"july-22-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-22', 'july-22-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-22-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"answers","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A diner enthusiastically enjoys yakiniku. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「はい、焼肉が好きです。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A diner enthusiastically enjoys yakiniku. That directly matches “Yes, I do. I like yakiniku.” (はい、焼肉が好きです。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「はい、焼肉が好きです。」という場面を表しています。そのため「Yes, I do. I like yakiniku.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Yes, I do. I like yakiniku.","jp":"はい、焼肉が好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Would you be available on August 4th at 10 a.m.?","jp":"8月4日午前10時はご都合いかがですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Neither is okay.","jp":"どちらも駄目です。"},{"id":"d","en":"Night shifts are still better.","jp":"それでも夜勤の方がまだいいです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-22-05-likes-yakiniku.webp","imageAlt":"A diner enthusiastically enjoys yakiniku.","visualAssetId":"july-22-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-23', 'july-23-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-23-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “まだ一つも思いついていません。”.","hintJa":"「まだ一つも思いついていません。」を表す英文と、present perfectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I haven’t thought of one yet.” is the sentence that means “まだ一つも思いついていません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I haven’t thought of one yet.」が「まだ一つも思いついていません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: まだ一つも思いついていません。","promptJa":"「まだ一つも思いついていません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I haven’t thought of one yet.","jp":"まだ一つも思いついていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m feeling under the weather.","jp":"少し体調がよくありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"A car suddenly appeared.","jp":"車が突然現れました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I just got home.","jp":"たった今家に着きました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-23', 'july-23-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-23-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"health","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the health meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “少し体調がよくありません。”.","hintJa":"「少し体調がよくありません。」を表す英文と、healthの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I’m feeling under the weather.” is the sentence that means “少し体調がよくありません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’m feeling under the weather.」が「少し体調がよくありません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 少し体調がよくありません。","promptJa":"「少し体調がよくありません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m feeling under the weather.","jp":"少し体調がよくありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"It’s too hot to go outside.","jp":"暑すぎて外に出られません。"},{"id":"c","en":"It fell on the floor.","jp":"それは床に落ちました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I ordered a chicken-and-egg rice bowl.","jp":"親子丼を注文しました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
