    ('july-23', 'july-23-draft-speaking-5', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-23-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"Doraemon","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the Doraemon meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ドラえもんは猫型ロボットです。”.","hintJa":"「ドラえもんは猫型ロボットです。」を表す英文と、Doraemonの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Model: “Doraemon is a cat-shaped robot.” (ドラえもんは猫型ロボットです。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Doraemon is a cat-shaped robot.」（ドラえもんは猫型ロボットです。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Doraemon is a cat-shaped robot.","speakJa":"ドラえもんは猫型ロボットです。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-23', 'july-23-draft-dialogue', 23, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-23-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"food","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the food meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “親子丼を注文しました。”.","hintJa":"「親子丼を注文しました。」を表す英文と、foodの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I ordered a chicken-and-egg rice bowl.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I ordered a chicken-and-egg rice bowl.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: What did you order for lunch?\nB: ...","contextJa":"A：「昼食に何を注文しましたか？」\nB：…","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I ordered a chicken-and-egg rice bowl.","jp":"親子丼を注文しました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Doraemon is a cat-shaped robot.","jp":"ドラえもんは猫型ロボットです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m feeling under the weather.","jp":"少し体調がよくありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"It fell on the floor.","jp":"それは床に落ちました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-23', 'july-23-draft-mistake', 24, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-23-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"Doraemon","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the Doraemon meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ドラえもんは猫型ロボットです。”.","hintJa":"「ドラえもんは猫型ロボットです。」を表す英文と、Doraemonの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “Doraemon is a cat-shaped robot.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「Doraemon is a cat-shaped robot.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"Doraemon a cat-shaped robot.","accepted":["Doraemon is a cat-shaped robot."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-23', 'july-23-draft-situation', 25, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-23-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"Doraemon","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the Doraemon meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どこでもドアならどこへでも行けます。”.","hintJa":"「どこでもドアならどこへでも行けます。」を表す英文と、Doraemonの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“The Anywhere Door can take you anywhere.” directly expresses “どこでもドアならどこへでも行けます。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「The Anywhere Door can take you anywhere.」が「どこでもドアならどこへでも行けます。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: どこでもドアならどこへでも行けます。","promptJa":"「どこでもドアならどこへでも行けます。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The Anywhere Door can take you anywhere.","jp":"どこでもドアならどこへでも行けます。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t thought of one yet.","jp":"まだ一つも思いついていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve just ordered lunch.","jp":"たった今昼食を注文しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I put it on the floor.","jp":"それを床に置きました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-23', 'july-23-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-23-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"health","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person feels mildly ill at home. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「少し体調がよくありません。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person feels mildly ill at home. That directly matches “I’m feeling under the weather.” (少し体調がよくありません。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「少し体調がよくありません。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I’m feeling under the weather.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m feeling under the weather.","jp":"少し体調がよくありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"It’s too hot to go outside.","jp":"暑すぎて外に出られません。"},{"id":"c","en":"It fell on the floor.","jp":"それは床に落ちました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I ordered a chicken-and-egg rice bowl.","jp":"親子丼を注文しました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-23-01-under-weather.webp","imageAlt":"A person feels mildly ill at home.","visualAssetId":"july-23-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
