    ('july-25', 'july-25-draft-visual-1', 26, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-25-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"getting","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person gradually starts to feel hungry before lunch. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「お腹が空いてきました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person gradually starts to feel hungry before lunch. That directly matches “I’m getting hungry.” (お腹が空いてきました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「お腹が空いてきました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I’m getting hungry.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m getting hungry.","jp":"お腹が空いてきました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m frustrated because nothing is working.","jp":"何もうまくいかず、もどかしいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"It’s getting cold.","jp":"寒くなってきました。"},{"id":"d","en":"No one knows the answer.","jp":"誰も答えを知りません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-25-01-getting-hungry.webp","imageAlt":"A person gradually starts to feel hungry before lunch.","visualAssetId":"july-25-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-25', 'july-25-draft-visual-2', 27, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-25-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"hunger","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: An extremely hungry person waits at an empty table. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「もう腹ペコです。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: An extremely hungry person waits at an empty table. That directly matches “I’m starving.” (もう腹ペコです。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「もう腹ペコです。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I’m starving.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m starving.","jp":"もう腹ペコです。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m annoyed by the noise.","jp":"その音にイライラしています。"},{"id":"c","en":"He’s making me nervous.","jp":"彼のせいで不安になっています。"},{"id":"d","en":"Is anyone there?","jp":"誰かいますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-25-02-starving.webp","imageAlt":"An extremely hungry person waits at an empty table.","visualAssetId":"july-25-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-25', 'july-25-draft-visual-3', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-25-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"feelings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person is annoyed by loud construction noise. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「その音にイライラしています。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person is annoyed by loud construction noise. That directly matches “I’m annoyed by the noise.” (その音にイライラしています。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「その音にイライラしています。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I’m annoyed by the noise.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m annoyed by the noise.","jp":"その音にイライラしています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m frustrated because nothing is working.","jp":"何もうまくいかず、もどかしいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"It’s getting cold.","jp":"寒くなってきました。"},{"id":"d","en":"No one knows the answer.","jp":"誰も答えを知りません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-25-03-annoyed-noise.webp","imageAlt":"A person is annoyed by loud construction noise.","visualAssetId":"july-25-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-25', 'july-25-draft-visual-4', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-25-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"nerves","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: Repeated phone notifications are getting on a person''s nerves. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「彼にはだんだんイライラしてきました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: Repeated phone notifications are getting on a person''s nerves. That directly matches “He’s getting on my nerves.” (彼にはだんだんイライラしてきました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「彼にはだんだんイライラしてきました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「He’s getting on my nerves.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He’s getting on my nerves.","jp":"彼にはだんだんイライラしてきました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m starving.","jp":"もう腹ペコです。"},{"id":"c","en":"Have you ever been hypnotized?","jp":"催眠をかけられたことがありますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"No one knows the answer.","jp":"誰も答えを知りません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-25-04-on-my-nerves.webp","imageAlt":"Repeated phone notifications are getting on a person''s nerves.","visualAssetId":"july-25-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-25', 'july-25-draft-visual-5', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-25-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"intuition","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A person trusts a bad gut feeling before entering a dark alley. Choose the sentence that describes that complete scene.","hintJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物を確認し、「何かがおかしい気がします。」に合う場面か考えましょう。場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A person trusts a bad gut feeling before entering a dark alley. That directly matches “I have a gut feeling that something is wrong.” (何かがおかしい気がします。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"イラストの人物の動作や物が「何かがおかしい気がします。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I have a gut feeling that something is wrong.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面を表します。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I have a gut feeling that something is wrong.","jp":"何かがおかしい気がします。"},{"id":"b","en":"Is anyone there?","jp":"誰かいますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m getting hungry.","jp":"お腹が空いてきました。"},{"id":"d","en":"He’s getting on my nerves.","jp":"彼にはだんだんイライラしてきました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-25-05-gut-feeling.webp","imageAlt":"A person trusts a bad gut feeling before entering a dark alley.","visualAssetId":"july-25-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-26-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"hope","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the hope meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。”.","hintJa":"「来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。」を表す英文と、hopeの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.” is the sentence that means “来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.」が「来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。","promptJa":"「来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアへ行けるといいな。"},{"id":"b","en":"I wish I were in Malaysia now.","jp":"今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"もう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I had finished dinner before he called.","jp":"彼が電話する前に夕食を終えていました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-26-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"wish","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the wish meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。”.","hintJa":"「今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。」を表す英文と、wishの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I wish I were in Malaysia now.” is the sentence that means “今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I wish I were in Malaysia now.」が「今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。","promptJa":"「今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I were in Malaysia now.","jp":"今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。"},{"id":"b","en":"I wish I had studied harder.","jp":"もっと勉強しておけばよかった。"},{"id":"c","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"まだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I had already eaten when you arrived.","jp":"あなたが到着した時にはもう食べていました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-26-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"regret","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the regret meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もっと勉強しておけばよかった。”.","hintJa":"「もっと勉強しておけばよかった。」を表す英文と、regretの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I wish I had studied harder.” is the sentence that means “もっと勉強しておけばよかった。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I wish I had studied harder.」が「もっと勉強しておけばよかった。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: もっと勉強しておけばよかった。","promptJa":"「もっと勉強しておけばよかった。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I had studied harder.","jp":"もっと勉強しておけばよかった。"},{"id":"b","en":"I wish I had been born there.","jp":"そこで生まれていたらよかった。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve just arrived home.","jp":"たった今家に着きました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"まだお風呂に入っていません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-26-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"past perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そこで生まれていたらよかった。”.","hintJa":"「そこで生まれていたらよかった。」を表す英文と、past perfectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I wish I had been born there.” is the sentence that means “そこで生まれていたらよかった。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I wish I had been born there.」が「そこで生まれていたらよかった。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: そこで生まれていたらよかった。","promptJa":"「そこで生まれていたらよかった。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I had been born there.","jp":"そこで生まれていたらよかった。"},{"id":"b","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"もう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have lived here since 2016.","jp":"2016年からここに住んでいます。"},{"id":"d","en":"I didn’t take a bath last night.","jp":"昨夜はお風呂に入りませんでした。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-26-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう朝食を食べました。”.","hintJa":"「もう朝食を食べました。」を表す英文と、present perfectの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"True. “I have already eaten breakfast.” means “もう朝食を食べました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「I have already eaten breakfast.」は「もう朝食を食べました。」という意味です。","prompt":"“I have already eaten breakfast.” means “もう朝食を食べました。”.","promptJa":"「I have already eaten breakfast.」は「もう朝食を食べました。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"july-26-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"yet","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the yet meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “まだ夕食を食べていません。”.","hintJa":"「まだ夕食を食べていません。」を表す英文と、yetの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"False. “I haven’t eaten dinner yet.” means “まだ夕食を食べていません。”, not “たった今家に着きました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I haven’t eaten dinner yet.」は「まだ夕食を食べていません。」であり、「たった今家に着きました。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I haven’t eaten dinner yet.” means “たった今家に着きました。”.","promptJa":"「I haven’t eaten dinner yet.」は「たった今家に着きました。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-26-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"just","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the just meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “たった今家に着きました。”.","hintJa":"「たった今家に着きました。」を表す英文と、justの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I’ve just arrived home.”. It expresses “たった今家に着きました。” with the lesson’s just pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I’ve just arrived home.」です。「たった今家に着きました。」を今回のjust表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: たった今家に着きました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：たった今家に着きました。","accepted":["I’ve just arrived home."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-26', 'july-26-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"july-26-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"since","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the since meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “2016年からここに住んでいます。”.","hintJa":"「2016年からここに住んでいます。」を表す英文と、sinceの形に注目しましょう。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I have lived here since 2016.”. It expresses “2016年からここに住んでいます。” with the lesson’s since pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I have lived here since 2016.」です。「2016年からここに住んでいます。」を今回のsince表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 2016年からここに住んでいます。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：2016年からここに住んでいます。","accepted":["I have lived here since 2016."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
